  The normalize table the collector rewrites raw OTLP attributes with. Two rules hold it
  together: the application never normalizes — it sets only keys the generator knows, and a
  vendor key is passed through as a tag, not renamed — and normalization never invents, so
  every rename target here is a key that exists in the registry.

  Renames are resolved transitively: a key deprecated into a key that was itself later renamed
  maps straight to the final live key, so the collector never has to chase a chain. A cycle or
  a target the registry does not know is a generation-time error, raised by the JQ filter.

  netstandard2.0-compatible and NativeAOT-clean: switch statements over string literals, no
  dictionary allocation, no reflection, no JSON.
-#}
